0,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{1,}_{{↑}_{{j}^{\\text{th}}\\text{ position}}}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0,…).\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{x}_{i}{e}_{i}=0\n$$\n\nif and only if ${x}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of ${ℓ}^{1}$ of size $n,$ which imples that  ${ℓ}^{1}$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${R}_{3000}[t]$ and  ${\\text{M}}_{50\\times 60}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{3000}[t])=3\\,000+1=3\\,001,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{50\\times 60}(R))=50\\cdot 60=3\\,000\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376876 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376877 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376878 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376879 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376880 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1041 "selection" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376876 13194139535962 true] [17592186376875 1110 #uuid "04c0f25e-9b8c-51e2-91cf-86742a4cd75b" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376876 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376876 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376876 1111 #uuid "a002214a-87b7-5306-a09e-e542c73063d3" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376877 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376877 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376877 1111 #uuid "91057ccf-b96f-549d-8973-06280574b0f0" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376878 1034 "I only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376878 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376878 1111 #uuid "e50e90bc-0136-594f-8cf2-34d8ad575992" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376879 1034 "III only" 1319