"II only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376915 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376915 1111 #uuid "cca5d9c4-3442-56a4-ad2c-d72e0d98097e" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376916 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376917 13194139535962 true] [17592186376916 1089 "q-95239" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376916 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535962 true] [17592186376916 1100 "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\n- ${R}^{200}$\n- $R[t],$ the vector space of all polynomial functions in the variable $t$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{200}(R),$ the vector space of all $200\\times 200$ matrices over $R$" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376916 1113 #uuid "52012800-e718-588f-a79c-9254035c24b3" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376916 1145 "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- $R[t]$ is *not* finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of (polynomial) functions is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,\\,t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,…,{t}^{n}},\\,n\\in N.\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=0}^{n}{a}_{i}{t}^{i}=0\n$$\n\nfor all $t\\in R$ if and only if ${a}_{i}=0$ for all $i=0,1,2,…,n.$ Therefore,  for any  $n\\in N,$  there exists a linearly independent subset of $R[t]$ of size $n,$ which imples that $R[t]$ cannot have finite dimension.\n\n- ${\\text{M}}_{200}(R)$ and ${R}^{200}$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{200}(R))={200}^{2}=40\\,000,\n$$\n\n \nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}^{200})=200\n$$\n\nare both finite numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376918 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376919 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376920 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376921 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376922 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1041 "selection" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376920 13194139535962 true] [17592186376917 1110 #uuid "2776a324-97de-5aa8-be3e-813aa6d3b28a" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376918 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376918 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376918 1111 #uuid "3cf907f4-6b6f-560c-a19e-861b019de6e3" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376919 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376919 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376919 1111 #uuid "0c5a3a2e-139b-5282-86be-8c03b481d403" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376920 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376920 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376920 1111 #uuid "899e2062-6bb8-5049-8b5d-2dcd13d458b0" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376921 1034 "I only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376921 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376921 1111 #uuid "57dee912-3916-566b-ae8c-cb4eb0cfd114" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376922 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376922 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376922 1111 #uuid "81dcddfb-95aa-5f91-b89c-82c291d00108" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376923 1017 #edb/ref 17592186376924 13194139535962 true] [17592186376923 1089 "q-95240" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376923 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535962 true] [17592186376923 1100 "Which of the following vector spaces are finite-dimensional?\n\n- ${R}_{1000}[t],$ the vector space of all polynomials in the variable $t$ of degree at most $1\\,000$\n- ${\\text{M}}_{200\\times 500}(R),$ the vector space of all $200\\times 500$ matrices over $R$\n- $C,$ as a vector space over $R$" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376923 1113 #uuid "03206f5b-8fe5-5de2-9b76-68d8a9d6bf34" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376923 1145 "Let's examine our vector spaces.\n\n- ${R}_{1000}[t]$ and ${\\text{M}}_{200\\times 500}(R)$ are finite-dimensional. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({R}_{1000}[t])=1\\,000+1=1\\,001,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{dim}({\\text{M}}_{200\\times 500}(R))=200\\cdot 500=100\\,000\n$$\n\n \nare both finite numbers.\n\n- $C$ is also finite-dimensional. To understand why, we first note that the following set of complex numbers is linearly independent:\n\n$$\n{1,i}\n$$\n\nIndeed, we have that \n\n$$\na\\cdot 1+b\\cdot i=0\n$$\n\nif and only if $a=0$ and $b=0.$ Since our vector space is also spanned by this linearly independent subset, we have that $\\text{dim}(C)=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376925 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376926 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376927 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376928 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1000 #edb/ref 17592186376929 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1041 "selection" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1104 #edb/ref 17592186376925 13194139535962 true] [17592186376924 1110 #uuid "2a4ee5dc-d1aa-52fa-803f-e870bd84d783" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376925 1034 "I, II, and III" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376925 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376925 1111 #uuid "8ea024fd-cfc4-524a-8e01-5c85ee9f9576" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376926 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376926 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376926 1111 #uuid "969af205-2c6e-5119-a92f-7781a4cb884b" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376927 1034 "I only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376927 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376927 1111 #uuid "8556b682-a2e3-5c8a-b53c-0f18138bffb3" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376928 1034 "III only" 13194139535962 true] [17592186376928 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535962 true] [17592186376928 1111 #uuid "b51adb